  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Iraq Capstone Seminar 01-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In fulfillment of the theater security cooperation objectives of USCENTCOM and in support of the Office of the Secretary of Defense for Policy (OSD-P), the Iraq General Officers Seminar is intended to build stronger relationships with the GOI. The primary objective of the seminar is to promote dialogue and regional cooperation among leaders and national security implementers throughout the GOI. The seminar is intended to broaden participants understanding of timely security issues through engagement with distinguished scholars, U.S. policy advisors, and U.S. defense personnel. Some of the results will be unique insights gained from leaders in the region, as well as the creation of a professional network of government, military, and academic leaders better prepared to engage in the international community.The Iraq General Officers Seminar will provide a unique opportunity for participants to forge professional, international relationships. The seminar will offer a chance for policymakers, military officers, and academics to develop U.S. foreign policy recommendations utilizing regional participants perspectives and experiences. The program also provides an opportunity for professional development for the participants. During the seminar, all participants will be briefed on available NESA outreach tools and social media outlets. Faculty will encourage continued engagement beyond the program through future NESA programs, academic products, and media and communications.</narrative>
  </description>
